but, like, only one of them kills him, and the other guy's just stabbed in a dead body.

00:36:22.780 --> 00:36:24.380
Now, that's just the devil's advocate.

00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:30.540
I think, you know. No, I completely, I completely agree with that on the, like, functionality, what's actually happening here.

00:36:30.580 --> 00:36:38.100
When I play a Final Fantasy game, I, I don't imagine that they're actually standing in a straight line and waiting for their turn to attack and attacking.

00:36:38.280 --> 00:36:39.820
Like, I, and I get that functionally.

00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:44.740
But, me, the player, I am seeing it turn-based, and yes, like, I get it.

00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:49.160
Like, how would they know? But, like, I'd like to think that they're coordinated enough to make those decisions.

00:36:49.560 --> 00:36:51.500
But, well, apparently you weren't.

00:36:51.800 --> 00:36:54.640
I guess not. But this, this bothered me.

00:36:54.920 --> 00:36:58.980
But also, you know, it also did lead to different ways you got to think about it.

00:36:59.060 --> 00:37:02.560
And I don't know if this is really, like, I'm not going to say this is a feature and not a bug.

00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:03.480
It's definitely a bug.

00:37:03.480 --> 00:37:12.320
But, like, yeah, I did have to think about, like, how can I spread out the damage I'm doing to do the most damage without wasting a shot on anyone?

00:37:12.680 --> 00:37:20.460
Which is, works out well sometimes, but also other times it's, like, it would be nice to just, like, overkill this guy.

00:37:20.780 --> 00:37:24.600
But I never know if, like, I'm going to just waste a whole shot.

00:37:24.780 --> 00:37:31.340
So, like, it would be nice to, like, get less people on, you know, enemies on the screen right away by just, like, attacking one person.

00:37:31.340 --> 00:37:41.380
But I do end up saying, like, okay, my two hardest hitters are going to have to attack different enemies, even if they don't take out either of them and just lower their HP on the first two turns.

00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:44.880
So the next two turns they take out both of them, I'm not wasting a whole swing.

00:37:45.260 --> 00:37:47.080
Even if it's not a bug, right?

00:37:47.180 --> 00:37:49.000
Like, even if it is, like, oh, it's intended, right?

00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:52.980
Like, you shouldn't. Well, there's a reason they moved over to attack redirect, you know?

00:37:53.140 --> 00:38:01.640
Right, right. But that's what I'm saying is, like, there's never an implication for, like, a scenario where you shouldn't hit that other enemy, right?

00:38:01.740 --> 00:38:06.980
Like, there's never a, like, oh, and because you hit that enemy, now you're poisoned, right?

00:38:07.060 --> 00:38:10.880
Like, enemies can poison you, but not from physical attacks.

00:38:11.160 --> 00:38:18.800
So there's never a reason to say, like, oh, well, thank goodness he didn't accidentally deal some damage to the enemy behind him.

00:38:18.800 --> 00:38:20.940
It's like you always want to be dealing damage.

00:38:21.420 --> 00:38:28.880
But I do agree, though, with Joe's developer apologist answer.

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:34.960
Because, yeah, it does kind of create, intended or not, emergent strategy.

00:38:35.420 --> 00:38:46.020
Now, maybe if this game had more, like, less battles, I could have the patience for it.

00:38:46.020 --> 00:38:49.320
But you're going to be in this screen all the time.

00:38:49.780 --> 00:38:53.980
And I even just like, when you choose to, this game has random battles.

00:38:54.340 --> 00:38:58.500
Whether you're in a dungeon, the overworld, or whatever, you're going to keep falling into this.

00:38:58.560 --> 00:39:03.540
And unless you want to run away a lot, you're going to have to do this mental math each time you fight.

00:39:03.700 --> 00:39:08.400
And, you know, when you're grinding, you don't want to have to do this.

00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:12.940
So, yeah, they finally, they got together.

00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:15.800
They implemented attack, redirect somewhere down the line.

00:39:15.960 --> 00:39:17.080
Don't know if it was FF2.

00:39:18.160 --> 00:39:20.580
You guys would have the better answer for that.

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:28.240
Because, yeah, when I was talking earlier and said, like, great battle system, I kind of just meant the vibe, the UI.

00:39:28.620 --> 00:39:30.960
That is such a pain in the ass.

00:39:31.040 --> 00:39:32.580
It kind of spoils things.

00:39:33.360 --> 00:39:40.060
Yeah, that's why, I mean, I think that it would have spoiled things a lot more for me if I wasn't so reliant on my black mage.

00:39:41.240 --> 00:39:44.040
Because that made it so it's like you could do a lot of area of effect.

00:39:44.360 --> 00:40:09.380
Not worry about that. And is the combat system too simple compared to modern?

00:40:09.380 --> 00:40:14.440
Obviously, modern turn-based RPGs are mostly becoming ARPGs.

00:40:14.620 --> 00:40:22.000
But even just from a RPG of any kind of combat standpoint, is it too much of just, oh, do the physical attack if you're this guy?

00:40:22.220 --> 00:40:24.180
Oh, do the magic attack if you're this guy?

00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:28.720
Like, how varied can the individual battles become?

00:40:29.500 --> 00:40:40.260
It really turns into, like, you can tell by the philosophy that they kind of grant the higher level encounters.

00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:47.580
And that you kind of see foreshadowing early on when there's maybe just one enemy or two enemies in the screen.

00:40:47.740 --> 00:40:49.760
But they're, like, in the back, in the corner.

00:40:49.940 --> 00:40:52.740
And you're like, oh, God, is this whole field going to get filled up?

00:40:52.740 --> 00:40:55.640
And then, lo and behold, the whole field gets filled up.

00:40:55.860 --> 00:41:01.300
And really, the way that they kind of scale things at this, throw more enemies at you.

00:41:01.680 --> 00:41:08.160
And I think that shows you that the battle system is very simple.

00:41:08.320 --> 00:41:14.040
And there are, you know, there's status effects to be wary of.

00:41:14.040 --> 00:41:18.360
And there are strengths and weaknesses that these enemies have.

00:41:18.620 --> 00:41:26.440
But, like, there's no, like, interplay between enemies where one keeps healing the other.

00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:31.680
So you kind of have to prioritize this that you'll see in later games.

00:41:34.500 --> 00:41:39.760
There's, it's really just attrition when you're in these battles.

00:41:39.760 --> 00:41:40.800
I don't know if you agree.

00:41:40.800 --> 00:41:46.420
Yeah, I don't want to be rude to all turn-based RPGs at the same time.

00:41:46.640 --> 00:41:50.820
But it's amazing that we ever had the time to do all this.

00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:54.100
Like, we've all, we all played these kinds of games at some point in our life.

00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:59.420
And we all kind of agree to the contract of the game that this is the gameplay loop.

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:05.300
And eventually, you know, you probably, like, figure out a way to just zone out and do it.

00:42:05.380 --> 00:42:09.520
Or you just get so good at it that, you know, you don't mind the grinding of it.

00:42:09.520 --> 00:42:22.460
But it is kind of crazy now as an adult with a job and a family, you know, and, like, things to do outside of the, like, potential, you know, today I'm going to play Final Fantasy all day, right?

00:42:22.560 --> 00:42:24.880
Like, that used to be a thing that we could do.

00:42:24.880 --> 00:42:29.140
But now it's like, wow, how did we ever used to do that?

00:42:29.280 --> 00:42:34.160
Like, we, it's not even that it's so simple that it's bad.

00:42:34.160 --> 00:42:38.680
I do think that this is a great combat system for the NES's time.

00:42:39.760 --> 00:42:44.100
Especially because it does make each class of character feel unique.

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:46.900
Something that is a bit of a concern, right?

00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:53.200
That, like, well, what if everybody's just, like, this guy's holding a sword and this guy's holding a cane and this guy's holding a hammer, right?

00:42:53.220 --> 00:42:55.540
It's like, no, they actually do different things and it's fine.

00:42:55.960 --> 00:42:59.200
It's, you know, you can just make them attack, but they also have different roles.

00:42:59.200 --> 00:43:11.020
Here, I think it's just, especially with the grinding that's required, there is just a time commitment that needs to be recognized.

00:43:11.020 --> 00:43:22.860
Even just early on to get to the title screen role at the beginning of the game, which we'll talk about, just to get to that moment requires a fair amount of grinding.

00:43:23.540 --> 00:43:26.640
Yeah, grinding, I'm never a fan of grinding.

00:43:26.640 --> 00:43:33.880
But I just, I think this isn't a, what we're talking about isn't a problem with the battle system.

00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:41.560
It's a problem with encounter design, which can have a good battle system attached to bad encounter design.

00:43:42.060 --> 00:43:46.680
And when I say that, I mean, let's just throw a bunch of enemies at you.

00:43:48.280 --> 00:43:56.180
Now, when I say that that's not a problem with the battle system, that's not to say that this doesn't have problems in the battle system.

00:43:56.180 --> 00:44:04.780
I think that the fact that we, I think we need to acknowledge that the version of the game that we're playing is broken in many ways.

