02:22:39.400 --> 02:22:40.520
Well, what's the other one?

02:22:40.520 --> 02:22:41.880
Worm? Worm.

02:22:42.480 --> 02:22:45.040
Oh, yeah, yeah. So, those are in the game, right?

02:22:45.040 --> 02:22:45.900
I'm not making this up.

02:22:45.980 --> 02:22:47.460
I guess, yeah, those are dragons.

02:22:47.860 --> 02:22:49.340
I don't remember there being a wyvern.

02:22:49.780 --> 02:22:50.680
Yeah, I think there is.

02:22:51.420 --> 02:22:54.000
I think it's just the worm, but it's blue instead.

02:22:54.600 --> 02:22:57.440
Gotcha. I'm not saying, like, look, I know what you're saying.

02:22:57.480 --> 02:23:01.920
You're saying you fought a big dragon as, like, a boss fight or something.

02:23:02.200 --> 02:23:06.140
Like, that's what the FMV, the FMV wouldn't say, like, you know, okay, for the opening cutscene,

02:23:06.300 --> 02:23:09.980
let's have an epic fight with the heroes and nine goblins.

02:23:10.700 --> 02:23:12.240
That's not what they're going to write down.

02:23:12.660 --> 02:23:14.520
They're not promising that, you know?

02:23:16.120 --> 02:23:24.440
And moving along, then we have the mobile versions of Final Fantasy 1, which just added, like, the touch controls and stuff like that.

02:23:24.520 --> 02:23:30.720
But also, a controversial feature, even to this day, probably, the auto-battle feature.

02:23:31.280 --> 02:23:38.780
What do you think about auto-battling in a game where the balance wasn't intended for you to auto-battle?

02:23:38.780 --> 02:23:49.680
I think if you're trying to sell this to the kind of person that will play a game for the first time on a cell phone,

02:23:50.380 --> 02:23:54.740
you're probably going to want to put some pretty crazy quality-of-life features in there,

02:23:54.760 --> 02:23:57.000
because these people are playing the game on a commute.

02:23:57.000 --> 02:24:00.420
Or, you know, like, it's...

02:24:00.420 --> 02:24:06.300
Or if they're a fan, they don't particularly need to experience the grind.

02:24:06.540 --> 02:24:16.240
Like, I don't think that it's a crazy, like, sacrilege to put something like that into a mobile game.

02:24:16.240 --> 02:24:18.560
Yeah, I agree.

02:24:18.580 --> 02:24:25.000
And I've come full circle on this, or I guess 180 on this, from what my opinion used to be,

02:24:25.080 --> 02:24:26.620
because I used to be like, absolutely not.

02:24:26.620 --> 02:24:30.700
That is stupid. That's against the spirit of the game.

02:24:32.120 --> 02:24:35.240
But some of these where it's like, yeah, if you're just grinding...

02:24:36.440 --> 02:24:40.340
As long as the auto-battle doesn't actually help you in difficult battles,

02:24:40.360 --> 02:24:44.220
as long as it's just like, yeah, I'm going to just auto-battle through this to get some experience or whatever,

02:24:44.220 --> 02:24:48.160
I'm just going to have it on auto-battle until I get to a dungeon or something, you know,

02:24:48.240 --> 02:24:51.940
where, like, then suddenly you're at a disadvantage if you're auto-battling,

02:24:51.940 --> 02:24:53.660
and you've got to shut it off and you've got to actually make decisions.

02:24:53.840 --> 02:24:54.760
I'm okay with it.

02:24:54.820 --> 02:24:57.020
I'm okay with it to help with grinding.

02:24:57.640 --> 02:25:04.720
The NES Classic Edition version just takes the actual NES game and just puts it on the NES Classic.

02:25:05.080 --> 02:25:07.340
Works and all. Yep, everything included.

02:25:07.600 --> 02:25:10.400
So, wishful thinking if it was going to get any upgrades.

02:25:10.400 --> 02:25:18.860
And that leads us with the Pixel Remaster, which, you know, it has the ability to switch soundtracks

02:25:18.860 --> 02:25:24.560
between the PSP version and the original songs.

02:25:24.660 --> 02:25:29.740
It has some quality of life improvements, like the auto-battle feature from the mobile versions,

02:25:29.860 --> 02:25:35.280
but also just saying, hey, turn off encounters for a little bit.

02:25:35.280 --> 02:25:40.660
Like, you can literally just go on the menu and say, no encounters, and then just continue on your way.

02:25:40.780 --> 02:25:42.620
You can say, you know what?

02:25:43.060 --> 02:25:48.260
Experience? Give me, like, four times the amount of experience that you would have given me for each battle.

02:25:48.300 --> 02:25:51.840
Or you could say, just keep it the same, but actually, gill?

02:25:52.000 --> 02:25:55.080
Give me four times the amount of gill that you would have given me.

02:25:55.100 --> 02:25:57.880
You can balance the game however you personally please.

02:25:57.880 --> 02:26:02.660
And I think that leads to a pretty slippery slope, if you're not careful.

02:26:02.880 --> 02:26:09.000
But most importantly, for whatever reason, nobody asked for it, but the Pixel Remaster decided,

02:26:09.620 --> 02:26:12.320
Power of Peninsula stops here.

02:26:12.720 --> 02:26:14.420
And they removed it.

02:26:14.800 --> 02:26:21.820
The only version of the game that doesn't have the Peninsula of Power is the Pixel Remaster,

02:26:21.900 --> 02:26:25.960
which doesn't make sense, because they would have to go in and fix those three tiles.

02:26:25.960 --> 02:26:27.060
One thing, yeah.

02:26:27.460 --> 02:26:28.340
That's weird.

02:26:28.680 --> 02:26:30.020
But they said, you know what?

02:26:30.140 --> 02:26:30.940
To hell with it.

02:26:31.060 --> 02:26:32.280
We don't want it anymore.

02:26:32.280 --> 02:26:36.340
But go ahead and ask for four times experience upgrades.

02:26:36.780 --> 02:26:44.160
I think, going back to all of those features that, like, that you were mentioning about the most recent version,

02:26:44.660 --> 02:26:47.060
about, like, give me four times experience.

02:26:47.760 --> 02:26:49.440
I don't want to butt fight anything.

02:26:50.840 --> 02:26:54.660
I also think there might have been a point in this podcast where I would have, like,

02:26:54.980 --> 02:26:56.820
really been upset by something like that.

02:26:56.920 --> 02:27:02.860
But I think now, like, the games, like, if you want to experience the game the way that it's meant to be played,

02:27:03.720 --> 02:27:05.560
you don't have to use that stuff.

02:27:05.620 --> 02:27:07.020
And you probably shouldn't.

02:27:07.020 --> 02:27:17.580
But in just purely a video game, what's the word I'm looking for?

02:27:17.600 --> 02:27:19.260
Yeah, well, you're looking for the Yoshi mode.

02:27:19.480 --> 02:27:20.440
No, no, no, I'm not.

02:27:20.440 --> 02:27:24.720
You can't die, and, like, you just play as Yoshi, and nothing hurts you.

02:27:25.080 --> 02:27:26.360
No, I mean, like...

02:27:26.360 --> 02:27:27.900
The museum version of the game.

02:27:28.000 --> 02:27:29.740
Exactly. That's the word I'm looking for.

02:27:29.880 --> 02:27:31.320
You have a better word for it.

02:27:31.320 --> 02:27:35.700
It would be video game, not restoration, but...

02:27:35.700 --> 02:27:36.560
Preservation.

02:27:37.940 --> 02:27:41.340
That's it. I brain farted, couldn't find that word.

02:27:41.680 --> 02:27:43.360
But that's what it's there for.

02:27:43.640 --> 02:27:45.380
It's like, experience this.

02:27:46.520 --> 02:27:47.800
It has meaning.

02:27:48.840 --> 02:27:50.140
Play around with it.

02:27:50.520 --> 02:27:53.700
But the actual experience is also here if you want it.

02:27:53.940 --> 02:27:58.640
Yeah, I'm just not sure how much of the game exists once you turn off encounters

02:27:58.640 --> 02:28:02.500
and say, give me four times experience every time I fight things.

02:28:02.660 --> 02:28:07.160
Like, I'm just not sure how much of the game remains for Final Fantasy 1 in particular,

02:28:07.260 --> 02:28:08.220
you know? Yeah.

02:28:08.520 --> 02:28:14.520
I mean, I guess what you could do, and I can see myself even doing this, don't tell anyone,

02:28:15.140 --> 02:28:20.800
but is you could play through the main parts, but then when you get to a point where, like,

02:28:20.860 --> 02:28:25.400
okay, now this is a time where I would just do a bunch of grinding, like, and I don't

02:28:25.400 --> 02:28:30.600
want to do that because it's boring, turn experience up to 20 times, do three battles,

02:28:30.660 --> 02:28:34.040
and be like, okay, I did all that grinding, but I just got it out of the way much more

02:28:34.040 --> 02:28:35.680
quickly. I would have done it anyways.

02:28:35.680 --> 02:28:36.500
It would have happened.

02:28:36.640 --> 02:28:37.440
I just saved time.

02:28:37.660 --> 02:28:39.640
You know, however you gotta make yourself sleep at night.

02:28:40.240 --> 02:28:43.540
And then turn it back off and then play more of the game, you know?

02:28:43.780 --> 02:28:49.300
Yeah, there's shortcuts to, you know, show your son that won battles.

02:28:49.300 --> 02:28:52.160
Like, remember, like, this is what we used to do, son.

02:28:52.840 --> 02:28:54.060
I don't know what I'm doing.

02:28:54.740 --> 02:28:56.280
We've been talking for too long.

02:29:09.660 --> 02:29:13.820
You may be asking why this episode is so long, right?

02:29:13.980 --> 02:29:17.420
What are these guys, why do they want to talk about Final Fantasy so much?

02:29:17.540 --> 02:29:23.900
And that's because this is the only time we get to talk about Final Fantasy on Nostalgia.

02:29:23.900 --> 02:29:30.880
There will be no Final Fantasy 2, as we know it on the NES, or Final Fantasy 3.

02:29:31.440 --> 02:29:34.680
There is a Final Fantasy 2, which is technically Final Fantasy 4.

02:29:34.680 --> 02:29:36.000
It's all very complicated.

02:29:36.240 --> 02:29:41.800
But for the first time, I would like to explain that away.

02:29:42.120 --> 02:29:49.440
The notion of maybe why there was no Final Fantasy 2 Japan release in North America.

02:29:49.540 --> 02:29:50.900
Will you guys humor me?

02:29:51.500 --> 02:29:54.320
Sure. Yeah, this is the first time you're dropping this news.

02:29:54.320 --> 02:29:56.400
This is the first time it's ever been officially revealed.

02:29:56.420 --> 02:29:57.500
This is the first time it's ever been revealed.

02:29:57.860 --> 02:30:00.440
I'm making a compelling argument for it, okay?

02:30:01.200 --> 02:30:08.180
Okay. First, Final Fantasy 1 was released in 1987 in Japan.

02:30:08.540 --> 02:30:10.700
1990 in North America.

02:30:11.240 --> 02:30:18.920
And really, mostly a push on, like, you know, Nintendo's part after the success of Dragon Warrior and everything.

02:30:18.920 --> 02:30:28.220
So, you know, the delayed entry was mostly because RPGs weren't seen as something that would sell incredibly well in the States.

02:30:29.280 --> 02:30:31.560
We get Final Fantasy 1 on the NES.

02:30:31.560 --> 02:30:36.120
It's going to take time to find out if there's an audience there in the States for it, right?

02:30:36.780 --> 02:30:37.920
By that time.

02:30:37.920 --> 02:30:43.940
Final Fantasy 2 was released in Japan in 1988, okay?

02:30:44.340 --> 02:30:50.000
Final Fantasy 2 had more, you know, like, probably more advanced technology on some level or whatever.

02:30:50.160 --> 02:30:55.100
But I don't think that there is a technical limitation for the NES cartridge.

02:30:55.100 --> 02:31:07.600
Instead, I think that Final Fantasy 4, what we know as Final Fantasy 4 in Japan, Final Fantasy 2 for Super Nintendo, that's, like, that's coming.

02:31:07.780 --> 02:31:09.360
That's coming real fast.

02:31:09.660 --> 02:31:10.760
Final Fantasy...

02:31:10.760 --> 02:31:13.580
Yeah, that's true. Final Fantasy 4 is 1991.

02:31:14.520 --> 02:31:26.300
So, why would you waste your resources on debating bringing over Final Fantasy 2 and 3, where 2 wasn't even really that well received and 3 is now a older NES game,

02:31:26.360 --> 02:31:35.940
when you could be delivering Final Fantasy 2, your next big entry in the series for this new market in North America,

02:31:35.940 --> 02:31:42.980
as a Super Nintendo game, not that much longer after the release of Final Fantasy 1 on NES.

02:31:42.980 --> 02:31:53.080
I think this is where the lines get blurred a little bit, and people don't realize just how close we are to the release of the Super Nintendo.

02:31:53.260 --> 02:31:54.880
That's next year, right?

02:31:54.980 --> 02:31:55.940
Like, that's kind of crazy.

02:31:56.100 --> 02:31:58.080
1991, we're going to have the Super Nintendo.

02:31:58.740 --> 02:32:05.620
And we're going to have a Final Fantasy 2 slash 4 on our hands pretty quickly after that.

02:32:05.940 --> 02:32:06.840
Yeah, it makes sense.

02:32:06.960 --> 02:32:12.900
I mean, in terms of what would you rather use your localization resources on,

02:32:13.180 --> 02:32:23.400
I don't think that there's really an argument to be made for these older games when you have something brand spanking new right around the corner.

02:32:23.660 --> 02:32:33.340
And I don't know the exact date of when Final Fantasy 2 slash 4, like, came to America,

02:32:33.340 --> 02:32:43.280
but the latest I could think is 1992, considering it came out July 19th, 1991 in Japan.

02:32:44.120 --> 02:32:50.540
So, you know, again, that's only two years after the release of Final Fantasy 1.

02:32:50.540 --> 02:32:58.680
So you have to think the reason 2 and 3 didn't come is just because they wanted to move ahead and, you know,

02:32:59.200 --> 02:33:06.160
doing the kind of, like, Mega Man 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 all on the NES before Mega Man 7 on the Super Nintendo

02:33:06.820 --> 02:33:10.940
isn't, like, as solid a strategy as Capcom might want you to believe.

02:33:10.940 --> 02:33:14.940
And it's also not like they're serialized.

02:33:15.800 --> 02:33:22.320
Like, they're all their own story, so it's super easy just to slap a different Roman numeral on it.

02:33:22.320 --> 02:33:27.140
Yeah, don't you think that's actually the greatest thing about Final Fantasy as a series?

02:33:27.380 --> 02:33:29.640
Like, Dragon Quest can't say the same thing.

02:33:30.200 --> 02:33:34.320
Some of those games are trilogies, to my understanding.

02:33:34.500 --> 02:33:39.660
You play as the same, or, you know, you play the same main character, Erdrick or whatever,

02:33:40.300 --> 02:33:42.720
across, like, three different games or something like that.

02:33:42.840 --> 02:33:44.140
Yeah, they exist in the same world.

02:33:44.140 --> 02:33:50.760
Whereas the greatest thing about Final Fantasy is that every time they get the chance to start fresh,

02:33:50.920 --> 02:33:58.900
both story, game mechanics, and then there are just these tropes that we've been discussing with Chocobos, Moogles, all that,

02:33:59.100 --> 02:34:03.520
that they just get to continue to kind of, well, this is how we keep it Final Fantasy.

02:34:04.080 --> 02:34:05.220
I just love it.

02:34:05.440 --> 02:34:06.260
It's pretty hot.

02:34:06.540 --> 02:34:08.620
Yeah, I mean, I agree.

02:34:08.620 --> 02:34:15.560
That is my, there is just, it's hard for me to put my finger on, like, how much of this is just me being a fanboy,

02:34:15.600 --> 02:34:19.000
and how much of it is real, but, like, there's just something.

02:34:19.120 --> 02:34:23.820
When you hear, for a long time, when you hear a Final Fantasy story is coming,

02:34:24.660 --> 02:34:31.180
you know it's going to be its own new world, its own rules, its own lore, and it's,

02:34:31.780 --> 02:34:34.540
but it's still going to feel like a Final Fantasy.

02:34:34.720 --> 02:34:36.720
It's still going to have all these connected themes and everything,

02:34:36.720 --> 02:34:40.220
and that's why I'm always so excited to play a Final Fantasy that I haven't played,

02:34:40.400 --> 02:34:45.340
because it's, they're all these different stories, but they're all also these,

02:34:45.580 --> 02:34:52.360
this same level of, like, epicness to each of them, and, like, up until, yeah,

02:34:52.440 --> 02:34:54.580
what we were talking about, like, 11 through 15,

02:34:55.340 --> 02:34:59.920
you kind of always expect, like, a really high-quality story experience.

02:35:27.220 --> 02:35:29.140
And there's still people who are just like, hey,

02:35:29.140 --> 02:35:32.680
I still play 11 online to this day, you know,

02:35:32.840 --> 02:35:38.440
or people who defend 13, or defend, you know, 12 had, it's like,

02:35:38.560 --> 02:35:42.640
12 had, like, a weird run, and I feel like the Zodiac version really, like,

02:35:42.700 --> 02:35:45.360
helped it, you know, fall back into favor.

02:35:45.540 --> 02:35:48.060
I mean, people swear by 12, and I still really want to play it.

02:35:48.100 --> 02:35:51.460
Don't worry about doors lies. That's, uh, that's from the game, don't worry.

02:35:51.780 --> 02:35:52.780
It's all good.

02:35:52.780 --> 02:35:54.400
Yes. You should really play 12.

02:35:54.500 --> 02:35:56.380
I think 12 is fantastic.

02:35:56.720 --> 02:36:00.320
The Gambit system is another, like, you know, like we're saying,

02:36:00.420 --> 02:36:04.760
it's another really fun way of reimagining the Final Fantasy Combat system.

02:36:05.200 --> 02:36:07.360
Yeah. And that's the other thing.

02:36:07.500 --> 02:36:11.660
It's not just the story. They reinvent the gameplay system, like, every time.

02:36:11.980 --> 02:36:13.040
Like, they go really hard.

02:36:13.240 --> 02:36:16.800
Like, Final Fantasy 7 to Final Fantasy 8 to Final Fantasy 9,

02:36:16.880 --> 02:36:19.560
they're, like, completely different games, but they still feel similar.

02:36:19.560 --> 02:36:22.120
Yeah, if every game had materia, I'd be fine with it.

02:36:22.220 --> 02:36:24.920
If every game was the materia system, I'd be like, yeah, what's up?

02:36:25.540 --> 02:36:29.640
I wouldn't. I want them to keep changing things and evolving it and seeing, like,

02:36:29.740 --> 02:36:33.300
different ways to do similar things, you know?

02:36:33.420 --> 02:36:37.380
Like, that's what I love about them is, like, learning the new system.

02:36:37.620 --> 02:36:42.340
And two and three are different, and they were released in Japan,

02:36:42.340 --> 02:36:47.520
so there is a chance on our Nostalgia Bites podcast, which is only available.

02:36:47.520 --> 02:36:48.980
It's gonna happen. Just admit it.

02:36:49.100 --> 02:36:51.340
It's only available at patreon.com slash nostalgia.

02:36:51.340 --> 02:36:55.740
I don't know if it'll hit, like, two-plus hours of talking about those games,

02:36:55.800 --> 02:36:57.000
but, yeah, it's gonna happen.

02:36:57.120 --> 02:37:02.280
Sean's right. We're gonna play probably every RPG that never came out here on Nostalgia Bites

02:37:02.280 --> 02:37:04.060
because we just eat those things up.

02:37:05.680 --> 02:37:10.000
But, yeah, if you want to see that, the best way to tell us is on patreon.

02:37:10.220 --> 02:37:11.640
patreon.com slash nostalgia.

02:37:12.680 --> 02:37:19.980
And I think I feel pretty good about everything we talked about for Final Fantasy 1.

